  "live_records": {
    "q-348699": {
      "dom_id": "step-q348699",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}sin\\,(\\frac{x}{6})cos\\,(\\frac{x}{6})\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
