    "q-74412": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74412",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}))\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}))\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
